msgstr "내용 제목"

msgid "Custom"
msgstr "사용자 정의"

msgid "Required to grab the fields, or to have custom entity display as fallback display. If it has fields, be sure the selected \"View mode\" is enabled, and the enabled fields here are not hidden there."
msgstr "필드를 잡거나 사용자 정의 엔티티가 대체 화면으로 표시되게 하려면 필요합니다. 필드를 갖는 경우 반드시 선택된 \"보기 모드\"가 사용 가능하고 여기에서 사용 가능한 필드가 거기에서는 숨겨지지 않는지 확인하십시오. "

msgid "Manage view modes on the <a href=\":view_modes\">View modes page</a>."
msgstr "<a href=\":view_modes\">보기 모드 페이지</a>에서 보기 모드를 관리하십시오. "

msgid "Preload to optimize the loading of late-discovered resources. Normally large or hero images below the fold. By preloading a resource, you tell the browser to fetch it sooner than the browser would otherwise discover it before Native lazy or lazyloader JavaScript kicks in, or starts its own preload or decoding. The browser caches preloaded resources so they are available immediately when needed. Nothing is loaded or executed at preloading stage. <br>Just a friendly heads up: do not overuse this option, because not everything are critical, <a href=':url'>read more</a>."
msgstr "사전 로드는 늦게 감지되는 리소스의 로드를 최적화합니다. 일반적으로 대형 이미지 또는 hero 이미지는 fold 아래에 있습니다. 리소스를 사전에 로드하면 Native lazy 또는 lazyloader JavaScript가 시작되거나 자체 사전 로드 또는 디코딩을 시작하기 전에 브라우저에서 리소스를 발견하는 것보다 더 빨리 리소스를 가져오도록 브라우저에 지시합니다. 브라우저는 필요할 때 즉시 사용할 수 있도록 사전 로드된 리소스를 캐싱합니다. 사전 로드 단계에서는 아무 것도 로드되거나 실행되지 않습니다. <br>주의: 모든 것이 중요한 것은 아니므로 이 옵션을 과도하게 사용하지 마십시오. <a href=':url'>자세히 알아보기</a>."

msgid "Decide the `loading` attribute affected by the above fold aka onscreen critical contents aka <a href=':lcp'>LCP</a>. <ul><li>`lazy`, the default: defers loading below fold or offscreen images and iframes until users scroll near them.</li><li>`auto`: browser determines whether or not to lazily load. Only if uncertain about the above fold boundaries given different devices. </li><li>`eager`: loads right away. Similar effect like without `loading`, included for completeness. Good for above fold.</li><li>`defer`: trigger native lazy after the first row is loaded. Will disable global `No JavaScript: lazy` option on this particular field, <a href=':defer'>read more</a>.</li><li>`unlazy`: explicitly removes loading attribute enforced by core. Also removes old `data-[SRC|SRCSET|LAZY]` if `No JavaScript` is disabled. Best for the above fold.</li><li>`slider`, if applicable: will `unlazy` the first visible, and leave the rest lazyloaded. Best for sliders (one visible at a time), not carousels (multiple visible slides at once).</li></ul><b>Note</b>: lazy loading images/ iframes for the above fold is anti-pattern, avoid, <a href=':more'>read more</a>, even <a href=':webdev'>more</a>."
msgstr ""

msgid "The content image style. This will be treated as the fallback image to override the global option <a href=\":url\">Responsive image 1px placeholder</a>, which is normally smaller, if Responsive image are provided. Shortly, leave it empty to make Responsive image fallback respected. Otherwise this is the only image displayed. This image style is also used to provide dimensions not only for image/iframe but also any media entity like local video, where no images are even associated with, to have the designated dimensions in tandem with aspect ratio as otherwise no UI to customize for."
msgstr "컨텐츠 이미지 스타일입니다.이는 응답 이미지가 제공되는 경우 일반적으로 더 작은 글로벌 옵션 <a href=\":url\">응답 이미지 1px 플레이스홀더</a>를 대체하는 폴백 이미지로 취급됩니다. 응답 이미지 각각을 폴백 이미지가 되도록 하려면 잠시 비워 두십시오. 그렇지 않으면 이는 표시되는 유일한 이미지입니다. 사용자 정의할 수 있는 다른 UI가 없으므로 이 이미지 스타일은 지정된 치수를 가로 세로 비율과 함께 보유하도록 이미지/iframe뿐만 아니라 이미지가 연관되어 있지 않은 로컬 비디오와 같은 매체 엔티티에 대한 치수를 제공하는 데 사용됩니다."

msgid "Clear cache if lightboxes do not appear here due to being permanently cached. <ol><li>Link to content/ by Link field: for aggregated small media contents -- slicks, splides, grids, etc.</li><li>Image to iframe: video is hidden below image until toggled, otherwise iframe is always displayed, and draggable fails. Aspect ratio applies.</li><li>(Quasi-)lightboxes: Colorbox, ElevateZoomPlus, Intense, Photobox, PhotoSwipe, Magnific Popup, Slick Lightbox, Splidebox, Zooming, etc. Depends on the enabled supported modules, or has known integration with Blazy. See docs or <em>/admin/help/blazy_ui</em> for details.</li></ol> Add <em>Thumbnail style</em> if using Photobox, Slick, or others which may need it. Try selecting \"<strong>- None -</strong>\" first before changing if trouble with this complex form states."
msgstr ""

msgid "Supports both Responsive and regular images."
msgstr "응답 및 일반 이미지를 모두 지원합니다."

msgid "Allows different lightbox video dimensions. Or can be used to have a swipable video if <a href=\":photoswipe\">Blazy PhotoSwipe</a>, or <a href=\":slick\">Slick Lightbox</a>, or <a href=\":splidebox\">Splidebox</a> installed."
msgstr ""

msgid "Automatic will search for Alt text first, then Title text. Try selecting <strong>- None -</strong> first when changing if trouble with form states."
msgstr "자동은 Alt 텍스트를 먼저 검색한 후 제목 텍스트를 검색합니다. 양식 상태에 문제가 있는 경우 변경할 때 먼저 <strong>- None -</strong>을 선택하십시오. "

msgid "Multi-value rich text field will be mapped to each image by its delta."
msgstr "다중 값 서식있는 텍스트 필드가 그의 델타에 의해 각 이미지에 맵핑됩니다. "

msgid "Aspect ratio to get consistently responsive images and iframes. Coupled with Image style. And to fix layout reflow, excessive height issues, whitespace below images, collapsed container, no-js users, etc. <a href=\":dimensions\" target=\"_blank\">Image styles and video dimensions</a> must <a href=\":follow\" target=\"_blank\">follow the aspect ratio</a>. If not, images will be distorted. <a href=\":link\" target=\"_blank\">Learn more</a>. <ul><li><b>Fixed ratio:</b> all images use the same aspect ratio mobile up. Use it to avoid JS works, or if it fails Responsive image. </li><li><b>Fluid:</b> aka dynamic, dimensions are calculated. First specific for non-responsive images, using PHP for pure CSS if any matching the fixed ones (1:1, 2:3, etc.), <a href=\":ratio\">read more</a>. If none found, JS works are attempted to fix it.</li><li><b>Leave empty:</b> to DIY (such as using CSS mediaquery), or when working with gapless grids like GridStack, or Blazy Native Grid.</li></ul>"
msgstr ""

msgid "Usages: <ol><li>Placeholder replacement for image effects (blur, etc.)</li><li>Photobox/PhotoSwipe thumbnail</li><li>Custom works with thumbnails.</li></ol> Be sure to have similar aspect ratio for the best blur effect. Leave empty to not use thumbnails."
msgstr ""

msgid "<strong>Required for</strong>: <ul><li>image attribute translation,</li><li>lightboxes as image triggers,</li><li>(remote|local) video high-res or poster image.</li><li>thumbnail/ slider navigation association, etc.</li></ul>Main background/stage/poster image field with the only supported field types: <b>Image</b> or <b>Media</b> containing an Image field. Add a new Image field to this entity, if not the Image bundle. Reuse the exact same image field (normally <strong>field_media_image</strong>) across various entitiy types (Image, Remote video, Local audio/video, etc.) within this particular entity (says, Media). This exact same field is also used for bundle <b>Image</b> to have a mix of videos and images if this entity is Media. Leaving it empty will fallback to the video provider thumbnails, and may cause issues due to failing requirements above."
msgstr ""

msgid "Empty the value first if trouble with changing form states. The amount of block grid columns (1 - 12, or empty) for large monitors 64.063em  (1025px) up."
msgstr ""

msgid "<br /><strong>Requires</strong>:<ol><li>Any grid-related Display style,</li><li>Visible items,</li><li>Skin Grid for starter,</li><li>A reasonable amount of contents.</li></ol>"
msgstr ""

msgid "Only accepts uniform columns (1 - 12, or empty) for medium devices 40.063em - 64em (641px - 1024px) up, even for Native Grid due to being pure CSS without JS."
msgstr "JS가 없는 순수 CSS이므로 네이티브 그리드의 경우에도 중간 장치 40.063em - 64em(641px-1024px)의 경우 단일 열(1 - 12, 아니면 비어 있음)만 허용합니다."

msgid "Only accepts uniform columns (1 - 2, or empty) for small devices 0 - 40em (640px) up due to small real estate, even for Native Grid due to being pure CSS without JS. Below this value, always one column."
msgstr ""

msgid "How many items per display at a time."
msgstr "한 번에 화면당 항목의 수입니다. "

msgid "If checked, keys will be preserved. Default is FALSE which will reindex the grid chunk numerically."
msgstr "선택되면 키가 유지됩니다. 기본값은 눈금 덩어리를 숫자적으로 다시 색인화하는 FALSE입니다. "

msgid "Depends on the <strong>Display style</strong>."
msgstr ""

msgid "<br>Specific for <b>Native Grid</b>, two recipes: <ol><li><b>One-dimensional</b>: Input a single numeric column grid, acting as Masonry. <em>Best with</em>: scaled images.</li><li><b>Two-dimensional</b>: Input a space separated value with <code>WIDTHxHEIGHT</code> pair based on the amount of columns/ rows, at max 12, e.g.: <br><code>4x4 4x3 2x2 2x4 2x2 2x3 2x3 4x2 4x2</code> <br>This will resemble GridStack optionset <b>Tagore</b>. Any single value e.g.: <code>4x4</code> will repeat uniformly like one-dimensional. <br><em>Best with</em>: <ul><li><b>Use CSS background</b> ON.</li><li>Exact item amount or better more designated grids than lacking. Use a little math with the exact item amount to have gapless grids.</li><li>Disabled image aspect ratio to use grid ratio instead.</li></ul></li></ol>This requires any grid-related <b>Display style</b>. Unless required, leave empty to DIY, or to not build grids."
msgstr ""

msgid "Check this to turn the image into CSS background. This opens up the goodness of CSS, such as background cover, fixed attachment, etc. <br /><strong>Important!</strong> Requires an Aspect ratio, otherwise collapsed containers. Unless explicitly removed such as for GridStack which manages its own problem, or a min-height is added manually to <strong>.b-bg</strong> selector."
msgstr "이미지를 CSS 배경으로 만들려면 이것을 선택하십시오. 배경 커버, 고정된 첨부 등과 같은 CSS의 선행이 열립니다. <br /><strong>중요!</strong> 가로 세로 비율이 필요합니다. 그렇지 않으면 컨테이너를 접습니다. 자체 문제점을 관리하는 GridStack과 같이 명시적으로 제거된 경우가 아니면 최소 높이가 <strong>.b-bg</strong> 선택기에 수동으로 추가됩니다."

msgid "Requires a skin. The builtin layouts affects the entire items uniformly. Leave empty to DIY."
msgstr "스킨이 필요합니다. 기본 제공 레이아웃이 전체 항목에 균등하게 영향을 줍니다. DIY하려면 공백으로 두십시오. "

msgid "Skins allow various layouts with just CSS. Some options below depend on a skin. Leave empty to DIY. Or use the provided hook_info() and implement the skin interface to register ones."
msgstr "스킨은 CSS만을 갖는 다양한 레이아웃을 허용합니다. 아래의 일부 옵션은 스킨에 종속됩니다. DIY하려면 공백으로 두십시오. 또는 제공된 hook_info()를 사용하고 스킨 인터페이스를 구현하여 하나를 등록하십시오. "

msgid "Unless otherwise specified, the styles require <strong>Grid</strong>. Difference: <ul><li><strong>Columns</strong> is best with irregular image sizes (scale width, empty height), affects the natural order of grid items, top-bottom, not left-right.</li><li><strong>Foundation</strong> with regular cropped ones, left-right.</li><li><strong>Flex Masonry</strong> (@deprecated due to an epic failure) uses Flexbox, supports (ir)-regular, left-right flow, requires aspect ratio fluid to layout correctly.</li><li><strong>Native Grid</strong> supports both one and two dimensional grid.</li></ul> Unless required, leave empty to use default formatter, or style. Save for <b>Grid Foundation</b>, the rest are experimental!"
msgstr ""

msgid "If checked, SVG is not embedded in the IMG tag. Be sure to disable CSS background option. Only enable for CSS and JavaScript manipulations, and trusted users, due to <a href=\":url1\">inline SVG security</a>. Required <a href=\":url2\">SVG Sanitizer</a>."
msgstr ""

msgid "Sanitize the SVG XML code to prevent XSS attacks. Required <a href=\":url\">SVG Sanitizer</a>."
msgstr ""

msgid "Remove attributes that reference remote files, this will stop HTTP leaks but will add an overhead to the sanitizer."
msgstr ""

msgid "Force the fill to currentColor to allow the SVG inherit coloring from the enclosing tag, such as a link tag."
msgstr ""

msgid "Unlike images, SVG has no ALT and TITLE attributes, except for SVG Image Field, or core file Description field. This option will hide captions, and put them into image attributes instead. Relevant if Inline option is disabled aka using IMG tag. Be sure to enable them under the Caption fields."
msgstr ""

msgid "Input one of SVG dimension sources: <code>none, image_style, or WIDTHxHEIGHT</code>. To disable, input: <strong>none</strong>, and will also disable Aspect ratio option. The <strong>image_style</strong> ansich will use the provided Image style, useful to get consistent heights within carousels, or rigid grids. The <strong>WIDTHxHEIGHT</strong>, e.g.: 800x400, for custom defined dimensions. Default or fallback to extract from SVG attributes, unless <strong>none</strong> is set. Only width and height are supported. Affected by Aspect ratio option."
msgstr ""

